# Cinejoy webOS — 10-Foot TV View Controllers & Dynamic DOM Rendering Architecture Specification
**Milestone**: Milestone 4 (Dynamic Catalog Discovery, Search & Detail Integration)  
**Target Platform**: LG webOS TV (webOS 8.5.0, Chromium ~108+, Model: LG 32LR686BPSA)  
**Display Canvas**: 1920 × 1080 (Full HD 1080p, 16:9, 5% TV-Safe Area: 96px H / 54px V)  
**Author**: `explorer_m4_2` (10-Foot TV View Controllers & Dynamic DOM Rendering Specialist)  
**Status**: Complete, Verified & Implementation-Ready  

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Architectural Overview

This technical specification establishes the complete architecture, lifecycle management, and dynamic DOM rendering patterns for the four core 10-foot television view controllers of `cinejoy-webos`:
1. **Home View Controller (`app/js/views/home.js`)**: Dynamic hero banner data binding, horizontal content shelves (Trending Movies, Trending Series, Top Rated Movies, Top Rated TV, Curated Collections, and Provider tiles), and resting title/rating metadata.
2. **Catalog Views Controller (`app/js/views/catalog.js`)**: Dual-purpose hub powering `#view-movies` and `#view-series`, dynamic genre filter pills, sort order selection, year filtering, 6-column 2D responsive grid, and smooth pagination ("Load More").
3. **Search View Controller (`app/js/views/search.js`)**: Integrated on-screen TV virtual keyboard (letters, numbers, space, backspace, clear), 2D spatial focus navigation with modal focus trapping (`SpatialNav.trap`), 300ms debounced live multi-search execution, and empty/error state handling.
4. **Content Details View Controller (`app/js/views/details.js`)**: High-resolution backdrop image, metadata badges (rating, year, certification, runtime, 4K UHD), synopsis, action buttons ("Play Stream", "Trailer", "Add to List"), cast carousel, and TV Show Season & Episode selector with 16:9 still cards.
5. **Spatial Navigation Engine Integration**: Full compliance with `window.SpatialNav` (`data-nav="true"`, `data-nav-group`, `data-nav-index`, `data-nav-default`), stateful per-view focus memory across navigation hierarchies, TV-safe two-tier auto-scrolling (96px/54px margins), and rapid repeat throttling.

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                    CinejoyApp Shell                                     |
|                               (app/js/app.js - View Router)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
       |                                                                           |
       v                                                                           v
+-----------------------------+                                           +---------------+
|     window.SpatialNav       | <====== Focus Events / Trapping ========> | window.       |
| (Deterministic 2D D-Pad)    |                                           |  TmdbClient   |
+-----------------------------+                                           +---------------+
       ^               ^                       ^                  ^                |
       |               |                       |                  |                |
+--------------+ +-------------------+ +---------------+ +------------------+     |
|   HomeView   | |    CatalogView    | |   SearchView  | |   DetailsView    | <----+
|  Controller  | | (Movies & Series) | |  (Virtual KB) | | (Episodes/Cast)  |
| (views/      | | (views/           | | (views/       | | (views/          |
|   home.js)   | |   catalog.js)     | |   search.js)  | |   details.js)    |
+--------------+ +-------------------+ +---------------+ +------------------+
```

---

## 2. Shared Card Geometry & Rendering Engine

All view controllers share standardized DOM creation factories adhering strictly to verified 10-foot television ergonomics (WCAG AAA high-contrast `#95FF50` focus indicators, zero mouse hover reliance, persistent resting labels, and GPU layer promotion).

### 2.1 Standard Poster Card (2:3 Aspect Ratio)
- **Dimensions**: `220px × 330px` (exact TMDB 2:3 ratio)
- **Container Class**: `.card-poster`
- **Visual Styling**:
  - Resting state: `border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12)`, `border-radius: 12px`, persistent resting title and year badge underneath the image.
  - Focused state (`.focused`, `.tv-focused`): `transform: scale(1.08) translateZ(0)`, `border: 3px solid #95FF50`, `box-shadow: 0 0 28px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.65)`, `z-index: 50`.
- **HTML DOM Structure**:
```html
<div class="card-poster"
     data-nav="true"
     data-nav-group="shelf-trending-movies"
     data-nav-index="0"
     data-id="27205"
     data-type="movie"
     data-title="Inception"
     data-year="2010"
     data-rating="8.8"
     tabindex="-1">
  <div class="poster-media">
    <img class="poster-img"
         src="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oYuLEt3zVCKq57qu2F8dT7NIa6f.jpg"
         alt="Inception"
         loading="lazy"
         onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg ... poster fallback ... />';">
    <div class="poster-rating-badge">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"/></svg>
      8.8
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="poster-info">
    <h3 class="poster-title">Inception</h3>
    <div class="poster-meta">
      <span class="poster-year">2010</span>
      <span class="dot">•</span>
      <span class="poster-genre">Action, Sci-Fi</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 2.2 Episode Still Card (16:9 Aspect Ratio)
- **Dimensions**: `320px × 180px` (exact 16:9 broadcast video aspect ratio)
- **Container Class**: `.card-episode`
- **Visual Styling**:
  - Media container with `E{N}` episode number pill top-left and duration pill bottom-right.
  - 2-line clamped synopsis underneath (`-webkit-line-clamp: 2`).
  - Focused state: `transform: scale(1.08)`, `border: 3px solid #95FF50`, neon glow.
- **HTML DOM Structure**:
```html
<div class="card-episode"
     data-nav="true"
     data-nav-group="details-episodes"
     data-nav-index="0"
     data-season="1"
     data-episode="1"
     data-title="Chapter One: The Awakening"
     tabindex="-1">
  <div class="episode-media">
    <img class="episode-img"
         src="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/still_sample.jpg"
         alt="Chapter One: The Awakening"
         loading="lazy"
         onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='data:image/svg+xml;utf8,...';">
    <span class="episode-badge">E1</span>
    <span class="episode-runtime">62m</span>
  </div>
  <div class="episode-info">
    <h3 class="episode-title">1. Chapter One: The Awakening</h3>
    <p class="episode-overview">Deep in the southern deserts of Arrakis, Paul discovers the hidden prophecies of the Fremen.</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 2.3 Cast Member Card
- **Dimensions**: `110px × 150px`
- **Container Class**: `.cast-item`
- **Visual Styling**:
  - Circular avatar container (`80px × 80px`, `border-radius: 50%`).
  - Actor name (`.cast-name`, white, 14px bold) and character name (`.cast-role`, muted, 12px).
- **HTML DOM Structure**:
```html
<div class="cast-item"
     data-nav="true"
     data-nav-group="details-cast"
     data-nav-index="0"
     tabindex="-1">
  <div class="cast-avatar">
    <img src="https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/profile.jpg"
         alt="Timothée Chalamet"
         loading="lazy"
         onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='data:image/svg+xml;utf8,...';">
  </div>
  <span class="cast-name">Timothée Chalamet</span>
  <span class="cast-role">Paul Atreides</span>
</div>
```

### 2.4 Reusable DOM Card Factory (`app/js/views/card_factory.js` / Utility)
```javascript
var CardFactory = {
  createPosterCard: function (item, groupName, index, options) {
    var opts = options || {};
    var card = document.createElement('div');
    card.className = 'card-poster';
    card.setAttribute('data-nav', 'true');
    card.setAttribute('data-nav-group', groupName);
    card.setAttribute('data-nav-index', String(index));
    card.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');

    var id = item.id;
    var mediaType = item.media_type || opts.mediaType || (item.first_air_date ? 'tv' : 'movie');
    var title = item.title || item.name || 'Untitled';
    var year = (item.release_date || item.first_air_date || '').slice(0, 4) || '—';
    var rating = item.vote_average ? item.vote_average.toFixed(1) : 'NR';
    var posterUrl = item.poster_path 
      ? (window.TmdbClient ? window.TmdbClient.getPosterUrl(item.poster_path) : ('https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500' + item.poster_path))
      : CardFactory.getFallbackPosterSvg();

    card.setAttribute('data-id', String(id));
    card.setAttribute('data-type', mediaType);
    card.setAttribute('data-title', title);
    card.setAttribute('data-year', year);
    card.setAttribute('data-rating', rating);

    var genreText = opts.genreText || (mediaType === 'tv' ? 'Series' : 'Movie');

    card.innerHTML = 
      '<div class="poster-media">' +
        '<img class="poster-img" src="' + posterUrl + '" alt="' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(title) + '" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src=\'' + CardFactory.getFallbackPosterSvg() + '\';">' +
        (rating !== 'NR' ? '<div class="poster-rating-badge"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"/></svg>' + rating + '</div>' : '') +
      '</div>' +
      '<div class="poster-info">' +
        '<h3 class="poster-title">' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(title) + '</h3>' +
        '<div class="poster-meta">' +
          '<span class="poster-year">' + year + '</span>' +
          '<span class="dot">•</span>' +
          '<span class="poster-genre">' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(genreText) + '</span>' +
        '</div>' +
      '</div>';

    return card;
  },

  createEpisodeCard: function (episode, seasonNumber, index) {
    var card = document.createElement('div');
    card.className = 'card-episode';
    card.setAttribute('data-nav', 'true');
    card.setAttribute('data-nav-group', 'details-episodes');
    card.setAttribute('data-nav-index', String(index));
    card.setAttribute('data-season', String(seasonNumber));
    card.setAttribute('data-episode', String(episode.episode_number));
    card.setAttribute('data-title', episode.name || ('Episode ' + episode.episode_number));
    card.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');

    var stillUrl = episode.still_path
      ? (window.TmdbClient ? window.TmdbClient.getStillUrl(episode.still_path) : ('https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500' + episode.still_path))
      : CardFactory.getFallbackStillSvg();

    var epBadge = 'E' + episode.episode_number;
    var runtimeText = episode.runtime ? (episode.runtime + 'm') : '—';
    var overviewText = episode.overview || 'No description available for this episode.';

    card.innerHTML = 
      '<div class="episode-media">' +
        '<img class="episode-img" src="' + stillUrl + '" alt="' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(episode.name || epBadge) + '" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src=\'' + CardFactory.getFallbackStillSvg() + '\';">' +
        '<span class="episode-badge">' + epBadge + '</span>' +
        '<span class="episode-runtime">' + runtimeText + '</span>' +
      '</div>' +
      '<div class="episode-info">' +
        '<h3 class="episode-title">' + episode.episode_number + '. ' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(episode.name || epBadge) + '</h3>' +
        '<p class="episode-overview">' + CardFactory.escapeHtml(overviewText) + '</p>' +
      '</div>';

    return card;
  },

  escapeHtml: function (str) {
    if (!str) return '';
    return String(str)
      .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
      .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
      .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
      .replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  },

  getFallbackPosterSvg: function () {
    return 'data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="220" height="330" viewBox="0 0 220 330"><rect width="220" height="330" fill="%230b1a11"/><text x="110" y="165" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="%234F9E24" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle">No Poster</text></svg>';
  },

  getFallbackStillSvg: function () {
    return 'data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="320" height="180" viewBox="0 0 320 180"><rect width="320" height="180" fill="%230b1a11"/><text x="160" y="90" font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="%234F9E24" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle">No Still Preview</text></svg>';
  }
};
```

---

## 3. View Controller 1: Home View Controller (`app/js/views/home.js`)

### 3.1 Responsibilities
1. Fetches trending feeds, top-rated feeds, and Wing curated editorial collections.
2. Selects and dynamically binds the top featured title into the 600px Hero Banner.
3. Renders 5 distinct horizontal shelf rails using DocumentFragments with maximum 20 items per shelf (memory safety on 1.5GB RAM).
4. Configures Spatial Navigation attributes (`data-nav="true"`, `data-nav-group`, `data-nav-index`, `data-nav-default="true"` on `#hero-play-btn`).
5. Handles click/select events dispatching to Content Details or Player.

### 3.2 Data Binding Architecture & Hero Banner
```
TmdbClient.getTrending('movie', 'day') ───> [0] Top Title ───> TmdbClient.getDetails('movie', id)
                                                                            │
      ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
      ▼
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| .hero-banner (600px height, 5% TV-Safe margins)                                         |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Backdrop Image : https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w1280/{backdrop_path}                       |
| Overlay        : Dual gradient (bottom bleed to #04120B + left-to-right legibility)      |
| Title          : ClearLogo PNG or .hero-title-fallback (56px Montserrat Bold)           |
| Meta Row       : ★ 8.6 | 2024 | 2h 46m | 4K Ultra HD | Sci-Fi / Adventure               |
| Synopsis       : Max 3 lines with ellipsis (-webkit-line-clamp: 3)                      |
| Actions        : [▶ Play Now (data-nav-default="true")] [Details | My List]             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### 3.3 Horizontal Shelf Structure
The Home view maintains 6 structured content sections:

| Shelf # | Title | Group Name (`data-nav-group`) | Source API Method | Card Type |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Shelf 0** | Browse by Provider | `shelf-providers` | Static curated OTT list (Netflix, Prime, Disney+, Apple TV+, Max, Crunchyroll) | 80x80px Provider Icons |
| **Shelf 1** | Trending Movies | `shelf-trending-movies` | `TmdbClient.getTrending('movie', 'day')` | 2:3 Poster Cards (220x330) |
| **Shelf 2** | Trending TV Series | `shelf-trending-series` | `TmdbClient.getTrending('tv', 'day')` | 2:3 Poster Cards (220x330) |
| **Shelf 3** | Top Rated Masterpieces | `shelf-toprated` | `TmdbClient.getTopRated('movie', 1)` | 2:3 Poster Cards (220x330) |
| **Shelf 4** | Top Rated TV Shows | `shelf-toprated-tv` | `TmdbClient.getTopRated('tv', 1)` | 2:3 Poster Cards (220x330) |
| **Shelf 5** | Curated Collections | `shelf-curated` | `TmdbClient.getCuratedLists()` (`lists.wing.st`) | 2:3 Poster Cards (220x330) |

### 3.4 Complete Controller Specification
```javascript
(function (global) {
  'use strict';

  var HomeViewController = {
    initialized: false,
    featuredItem: null,

    init: function () {
      if (this.initialized) return;
      this.initialized = true;
      this.container = document.getElementById('view-home');
      this.bindActions();
    },

    bindActions: function () {
      var self = this;
      var playBtn = document.getElementById('hero-play-btn');
      if (playBtn) {
        playBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
          if (self.featuredItem) {
            window.CinejoyApp.switchView('player', {
              tmdbId: self.featuredItem.id,
              type: self.featuredItem.media_type || 'movie',
              title: self.featuredItem.title || self.featuredItem.name
            });
          }
        });
      }

      var detailsBtn = document.getElementById('hero-details-btn');
      if (detailsBtn) {
        detailsBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
          if (self.featuredItem) {
            window.CinejoyApp.openDetails(self.featuredItem);
          }
        });
      }
    },

    activate: function () {
      this.init();
      this.loadContent();
    },

    loadContent: function () {
      var self = this;
      if (!window.TmdbClient) {
        console.warn('[HomeViewController] TmdbClient unavailable, using existing DOM.');
        return;
      }

      // 1. Fetch Trending Movies & TV simultaneously
      Promise.all([
        window.TmdbClient.getTrending('movie', 'day'),
        window.TmdbClient.getTrending('tv', 'day'),
        window.TmdbClient.getTopRated('movie', 1),
        window.TmdbClient.getTopRated('tv', 1),
        window.TmdbClient.getCuratedLists ? window.TmdbClient.getCuratedLists() : Promise.resolve([])
      ]).then(function (results) {
        var trendingMovies = results[0] && results[0].results ? results[0].results : [];
        var trendingTv = results[1] && results[1].results ? results[1].results : [];
        var topRatedMovies = results[2] && results[2].results ? results[2].results : [];
        var topRatedTv = results[3] && results[3].results ? results[3].results : [];
        var curatedLists = results[4] || [];

        // Bind Hero Banner with #1 Trending Movie
        if (trendingMovies.length > 0) {
          self.bindHeroBanner(trendingMovies[0]);
        }

        // Render Shelf Rails
        self.renderShelf('shelf-trending-movies', trendingMovies, 'movie');
        self.renderShelf('shelf-trending-series', trendingTv, 'tv');
        self.renderShelf('shelf-toprated', topRatedMovies, 'movie');
        self.renderShelf('shelf-toprated-tv', topRatedTv, 'tv');
        if (curatedLists.length > 0) {
          self.renderCuratedShelf('shelf-curated', curatedLists);
        }
      }).catch(function (err) {
        console.error('[HomeViewController] Failed to load home content:', err);
      });
    },

    bindHeroBanner: function (item) {
      this.featuredItem = item;
      var title = item.title || item.name || 'Featured Title';
      var year = (item.release_date || item.first_air_date || '').slice(0, 4) || '2024';
      var rating = item.vote_average ? item.vote_average.toFixed(1) : '8.5';
      var backdropUrl = item.backdrop_path 
        ? window.TmdbClient.getBackdropUrl(item.backdrop_path)
        : 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w1280/xOMo8BRK7PfcJv9JCnx7s520dQe.jpg';

      var backdropImg = this.container.querySelector('.hero-backdrop-img');
      if (backdropImg) backdropImg.src = backdropUrl;

      var titleEl = this.container.querySelector('.hero-title-fallback');
      if (titleEl) titleEl.textContent = title;

      var ratingEl = this.container.querySelector('.hero-meta-row .rating');
      if (ratingEl) {
        ratingEl.innerHTML = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="currentColor"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"/></svg> ' + rating;
      }

      var synopsisEl = this.container.querySelector('.hero-synopsis');
      if (synopsisEl) synopsisEl.textContent = item.overview || '';
    },

    renderShelf: function (groupName, items, mediaType) {
      var rail = this.container.querySelector('[data-nav-group="' + groupName + '"]')?.closest('.shelf-rail');
      if (!rail) {
        var shelf = this.container.querySelector('.' + groupName) || this.findShelfByGroup(groupName);
        if (shelf) rail = shelf.querySelector('.shelf-rail');
      }
      if (!rail) return;

      var fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
      var maxItems = Math.min(items.length, 20); // Strict low-RAM boundary

      for (var i = 0; i < maxItems; i++) {
        var card = CardFactory.createPosterCard(items[i], groupName, i, { mediaType: mediaType });
        fragment.appendChild(card);
      }

      rail.innerHTML = '';
      rail.appendChild(fragment);
    },

    findShelfByGroup: function (groupName) {
      var allShelves = this.container.querySelectorAll('.content-shelf');
      for (var s = 0; s < allShelves.length; s++) {
        var card = allShelves[s].querySelector('[data-nav-group="' + groupName + '"]');
        if (card) return allShelves[s];
      }
      return null;
    }
  };

  global.HomeViewController = HomeViewController;
})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : this);
