## 7. Integration with `window.SpatialNav`

The view controllers coordinate seamlessly with `window.SpatialNav` through standardized HTML data attributes, focus memory contracts, auto-scrolling margins, and focus trapping:

### 7.1 Attribute Rules Matrix

| Attribute | Syntax | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `data-nav` | `"true"` \| `"false"` | Yes | Dictates whether element participates in candidate discovery. |
| `data-nav-group` | String (e.g. `shelf-trending-movies`) | Yes | Semantically groups elements for spatial memory and query filtering. |
| `data-nav-index` | Integer String (`"0"`, `"1"`, ...) | Recommended | Defines ordinal sequence inside shelves and grids. Index 0 resets shelf scrollLeft. |
| `data-nav-default`| `"true"` | Yes (1 per view) | Specifies primary default focus target when view memory is empty. |
| `data-scroll-rail`| `"true"` | Optional | Marks container as horizontal shelf rail for auto-scroll tracking. |
| `data-title` | String | Recommended | Used for fuzzy memory restoration if element is re-rendered with new ID. |

### 7.2 Focus Memory Preservation During View Switching
When transitioning between views (e.g. `Home -> Details -> Player -> Details -> Home`), `SpatialNav` implements a 6-tier resolution cascade:
1. Direct DOM node identity (`mem.element`)
2. Element ID (`mem.id`)
3. Group + Index (`[data-nav-group="..."][data-nav-index="..."]`)
4. Group + Title (`[data-nav-group="..."][data-title="..."]`)
5. View Default (`[data-nav-default="true"]`)
6. First navigable element in active view (`.view.active [data-nav="true"]`)

The view controllers hook into `CinejoyApp.switchView(targetView, data)`:
```javascript
// In CinejoyApp.switchView:
if (this.state.currentView && window.SpatialNav) {
  window.SpatialNav.saveFocus(this.state.currentView);
}

// ... activate new view ...

// Invoke view controller activate hook:
if (targetView === 'home' && window.HomeViewController) {
  window.HomeViewController.activate();
} else if (targetView === 'movies' && window.MoviesViewController) {
  window.MoviesViewController.activate();
} else if (targetView === 'series' && window.SeriesViewController) {
  window.SeriesViewController.activate();
} else if (targetView === 'search' && window.SearchViewController) {
  window.SearchViewController.activate();
} else if (targetView === 'details' && window.DetailsViewController) {
  window.DetailsViewController.activate(data);
}

// Restore focus after DOM settling:
window.SpatialNav.restoreFocus(targetView);
```

### 7.3 Two-Tier TV-Safe Auto-Scroll Coordinates
- **Horizontal Shelf Rail**:
  - `SAFE_X_MIN`: `96px`
  - `SAFE_X_MAX`: `1824px` (`1920 - 96`)
  - `PEEK_OFFSET`: `48px`
  - Rule: If `rect.left < 96px`, scrolls left by `96 - rect.left`. If `rect.right > 1824px`, scrolls right by `(rect.right - 1824) + 48`. Index 0 resets to `left: 0`.
- **Vertical Viewport**:
  - `EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN`: `104px` (84px fixed header + 20px buffer)
  - `SAFE_Y_MAX`: `1026px` (`1080 - 54`)
  - Rule: If shelf top < 104px, pane scrolls up. If card bottom > 1026px, pane scrolls down with 36px bottom buffer.

